tribes-communities.synthesis:
- Dominant form = **pair/match/elimination**, not descriptive anthropology.
- Highest-value memory structure: **Community → region → livelihood/practice → language**.
- Common traps:
  - adjacent-region swaps: Karbi→Himachal, Khas→Arunachal, Maasai→West Africa;
  - same-family spelling/OCR: Kirghiz/Kyrgyz, Paliyan/Palliyan, Keria/Kharia;
  - livelihood swaps: hunter-gatherer vs pastoral nomad;
  - island vs mainland tribe;
  - a cultural practice may be tested without naming the community directly (living-root bridges).
